{"id": "EUVD-2026-55280", "enisaUuid": "536deb98-e707-3e7f-881d-5c979e651174", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: nsm: only unlock nsm_dev on post-lock error paths\n\nnsm_dev_ioctl() jumps to the common out label even when the initial\ncopy_from_user() fails before nsm->lock has been taken.  The error path\nthen blindly unlocks a mutex that was never acquired.\n\nThis issue was found by our static analysis tool and then manually\nreviewed against the current tree.\n\nThe grounded PoC kept the miscdevice ioctl entry and the pre-lock\ncopy_from_user(&raw, argp, _IOC_SIZE(cmd)) failure path by issuing\nNSM_IOCTL_RAW with an invalid user pointer.  That failure reaches the\nshared out label before mutex_lock(&nsm->lock).  Lockdep reported:\n\n  WARNING: bad unlock balance detected!\n  exploit/193 is trying to release lock (&global_nsm.lock) at:\n  nsm_dev_ioctl+0x5f/0xcf [vuln_msv]\n  but there are no more locks to release!\n  no locks held by exploit/193.\n\nReturn immediately on the pre-lock copy_from_user() failure and keep the\ncommon unlock label for the post-lock paths only.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:59:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:58:56", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4aa3f7d48e91eb74a363c1b4d7dbdd28f5b341fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f068342096b027181b168d91fef7ac7a2c64b25", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f318f5a872cb9096536e759b23ae5c9873bb80ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce1fed11d18e163baf7f875152a33bf80f625c1a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3jf9-7qhv-4pm6", "CVE-2026-68179"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0170f927-cdc3-34c8-b54c-b650e7fd0df1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "0ffd025c-a142-3321-a5bf-ac9b5738b71b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <8f068342096b027181b168d91fef7ac7a2c64b25"}, {"id": "24bdec7e-ae9f-30cd-99b8-5043cee3f3cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <f318f5a872cb9096536e759b23ae5c9873bb80ed"}, {"id": "68d1e105-b187-3e95-8ca6-de41c2fd033e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "9e54bdc7-ea13-3562-835f-64782f5e998f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "ca78f33a-4dfc-3064-918f-5cf8286a1ff4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <ce1fed11d18e163baf7f875152a33bf80f625c1a"}, {"id": "cd8d185b-093a-3c76-9e11-d96443f555c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "e85bf802-0837-30fc-a5c7-d8e9a7b326fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "fa2625a9-cc44-39df-ba26-5ac73cac2e13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9873755a6c8ccfce79094c4dce9efa3ecb1a749 <4aa3f7d48e91eb74a363c1b4d7dbdd28f5b341fb"}, {"id": "fad8b7b2-1004-3488-8279-2f8e05ad8875", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d1f2c5ae-d753-39cb-a378-ebb56f618d1e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}